        <p>I'm currently working through the FlyRank AI Fluency Internship, where I'm learning how to apply AI tools and IT Support fundamentals to real, practical tasks.</p>
        <p>My first hands-on project from this journey is the <strong>Career &amp; Learning Assistant</strong> — an AI agent I built to help organise internship assignments into clear checklists, recommend the best order to complete them, and flag anything unclear before I start work. You can read more about it below.</p><h3>Proof of Work</h3>

<p><strong>Problem:</strong> Internship assignment briefs can contain several requirements that are difficult to organise and complete in the right order.</p>

<p><strong>What I built:</strong> I built the Career &amp; Learning Assistant as a Claude Project using the Google Drive Connector. It helps break assignment briefs into clear tasks, create a completion checklist, recommend an order for completing the work, and identify missing or unclear information.</p>

<p><strong>My contribution:</strong> I designed the agent instructions and workflow, connected the project to Google Drive, tested it with different FlyRank documents, reviewed its responses, and refined the MVP based on the evaluation results.</p>

<p><strong>Tools:</strong> Claude Project and Google Drive Connector.</p>      </div>
